d_Ceremony%2C_H%26MS-13%2C_circa_1968.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Change_of_Command_Ceremony,_H%26MS-13,_circa_1968.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=109870467","extmetadata":{"ObjectName":{"value":"Change of Command Ceremony, H&MS-13, circa 1968","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"\"New Commander: Major Edgar A. House, right, receives the squadron colors from Lieutenant Colonel Paul L. Siegmund, August 12, during a formal change of command ceremony at Headquarters and Maintenance Squadron 13 [H&amp;MS-13], Marine Aircraft Group 13 [MAG-13], Chu Lai, Vietnam.  House saw duty in Vietnam in September 1963 with Marine Medium Helicopter Squadron 361 [HMM-361].  He began his current tour as executive officer of Marine Medium Helicopter Squadron362 [HMM-362] and participated in operations Fortress Attack II, Napoleon Saline, Scotland II, and Fortress Attack III (official USMC photo by Staff Sergeant P. L. Stacy).\"\n<p>From the Jonathan Abel Collection (COLL/3611), Marine Corps Archives &amp; Special Collections.\n</p>\nOFFICIAL USMC PHOTOGRAPH","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Archives Branch, USMC History Division","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},{"pageid":126355930,"ns":6,"title":"File:Vietnam Magazine Vol. I, Nº 2 1968.pdf","index":4,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":16020346,"width":1304,"height":1708,"pagecount":35,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Vietnam_Magazine_Vol._I%2C_N%C2%BA_2_1968.pdf/page1-1280px-Vietnam_Magazine_Vol._I%2C_N%C2%BA_2_1968.pdf.jpg?utm_so